# Project groups for tabrail. Copy to groups.conf next to tabrail.tmux, or point the tmux option
# @tabrail_groups at a file of your own. A new tab joins the group with the longest folder it was
# opened in or below, at any level (equal ones: the first line); prefix M, a drag or the right-click
# menu moves it. Tabs in none: Default. The sidebar shows the groups in line order; the menu's "New
# group…" adds lines here, "New subgroup…" (or a click on a header's +) one indented under the
# group's subtree. Dragging a group's row in the sidebar moves its line and its subgroups' lines:
# let go at or right of another group's header name, it nests under that group; left of the name or
# on a tab's row, it keeps its level, next to a sibling. Default never moves. Columns: name (one
# word), tint behind the group's row (#rrggbb; a group menu's "Colour…" sets it to one of the palette
# file's), icon, folders (optional; a new tab of the group opens in the first, without any in the
# first of its nearest ancestor that has folders, else home).
# A line indented under another makes a subgroup, any depth deep: its parent is the nearest group line
# above it with less leading whitespace (a space or a tab counts one). The sidebar shows the tree, each
# level one column further right; folding a group hides its subgroups too. Below, a tab opened in
# ~/src/website/shop joins Shop, one anywhere else in ~/src/website joins Website.
Website   #283147  ◆  ~/src/website ~/src/website-staging
  Shop    #3a344e  ✦  ~/src/website/shop
Infra     #3b2f2a  ▲  ~/src/infra
Notes     #2a3b2f  ●
